              "scriptDescription": "Manages an interactive projectile simulation. Inputs: references to angleDial and speedSlider objects (reads their current drag-derived values to determine launch angle in degrees, 0-90, and launch speed in m/s, 1-25), reference to the interactiveBall object to animate its position along a parabolic path using standard kinematics equations with gravity = 9.8 m/s^2, reference to trajectoryTrace object to render the path traced by the ball, and reference to rangeHeightReadout text object to display computed range and max height values. On launch trigger (e.g. a button tap or automatic loop), computes the trajectory analytically from the current angle and speed, animates the ball along the path in real time, updates the trace line as the ball moves, and updates the readout text with the calculated range and maximum height in meters. Resets the ball to the launcher position at the end of each run to allow repeated experimentation."
